{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-95738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+3}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}}.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-95738" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95738" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(\\sqrt{3}-1)\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})+C"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})+C"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95738" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95693" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{2{e}^{2x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{4x}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95693" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${e}^{4x}={({e}^{2x})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u={e}^{2x}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2{e}^{2x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2{e}^{2x}}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{e}^{2x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{4x}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2{e}^{2x}}{\\sqrt{{({e}^{2x})}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2u}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{2x}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95693" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-95693" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95693" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "