& =\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\,x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-95692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "7\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\,x)+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\,x)+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\,x)+C"] ["math" "\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\,x)+C"] ["math" "\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\,x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\,x)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-96964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-96964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $36{x}^{2}=(6x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=6x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡6x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-96964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-96964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-96964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡6x+C"] ["math" "6\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡6x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡6x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡6x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡6x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-96964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡6x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${e}^{2x}={({e}^{x})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u={e}^{x}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{({e}^{x})}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-95690" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95690" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2e\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{e}^{x}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}+C"] ["math" "e\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{e}^{x}+C"] ["math" "e\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95690" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-25}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-25}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{5}.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=5\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-25}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-95853" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95853" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡5x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡5x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95853" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $9{x}^{2}=(3x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(3x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡3x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-95850" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95850" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡3x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡3x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡3x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡3x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡3x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95850" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡3x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-49}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-49}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{7})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{7})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{7}.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{7}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=7\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-49}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{7})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot 7\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =7\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =7\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =7\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{7})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-95855" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95855" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "49\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{7})+C"] ["math" "49\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{7})+C"] ["math" "7\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{7})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{7})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{7})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95855" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{7})+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{8}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{8}})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{2}})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{2}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{2}}.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{2}})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{2}})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-95854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{2}})+C"] ["math" "-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{2}})+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{2}})+C"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{2}})+C"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{2}})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{2}})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95432" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95432" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $16{x}^{2}=(4x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=4x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡4x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95432" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-95432" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95432" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡4x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95432" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡4x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{21}{7-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{21}{7-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=3\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{21}{7-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{7}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1-{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that this result is subject to the condition $|\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}}|<1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-95865" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95865" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+C"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{7}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{7})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{7})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95865" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95864" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{12}{16-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95864" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{12}{16-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{3}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{4}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=4\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{12}{16-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1-{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that this result is subject to the condition $|\\frac{x}{4}|<1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95864" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-95864" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95864" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡3x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95864" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95863" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{5}{9-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95863" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{5}{9-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{5}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{3}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5}{9-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1-{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that this result is subject to the condition $|\\frac{x}{3}|<1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95863" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-95863" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95863" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{9})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{9})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95863" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{2}{4-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{2}{4-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{2}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=2\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{4-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1-{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that this result is subject to the condition $|\\frac{x}{2}|<1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-95866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{12}{1-16{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $16{x}^{2}=(4x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=4x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{12}{1-16{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =12\\int \\frac{1}{1-(4x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{artanh}⁡4x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that this result is subject to the condition $|4x|<1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-95858" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95858" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\operatorname{artanh}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{artanh}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "6\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡4x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95858" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\operatorname{artanh}⁡4x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{3}^{6}\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{6}\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-3}}\\,\\text{d}x=3\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{3}^{6}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $3$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $2\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{6}\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{3}^{6}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}}^{2\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}}^{2\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u{|}_{\\sqrt{3}}^{2\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =9(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡2\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{{(2\\sqrt{3})}^{2}-1})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}-1})) \\\\  & =9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{11})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2})) \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{11}}{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-95900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{11}}{2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}})"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{11}}{2})"] ["math" "9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{11}}{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}})"] ["math" "9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+11}{2})"] ["math" "9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{11}}{4})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{11}}{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-346519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{20}{25-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$artanh\\,(${{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-346519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "$$\n\nNote that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{20}{25-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{4}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C,\n$$\n\nthe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{5}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=5\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{3}{5}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{20}{25-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{4}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{3/5}\\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{3/5}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1-{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{3/5} \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{3}{5})-4\\operatorname{artanh}⁡0 \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{3}{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-346519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-346519" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-346519" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-346519" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-346519" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-350220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{40}{64-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$artanh\\,(${{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-350220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "$$\n\nNote that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{40}{64-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{5}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{x}{8})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C,\n$$\n\nthe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{8})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{8}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{8}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=8\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{40}{64-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{x}{8})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{3/4}\\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\cdot 8\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{3/4}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1-{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{3/4} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})-5\\operatorname{artanh}⁡0 \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-350220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-350220" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-350220" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-350220" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-350220" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-96968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+36}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-96968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+36}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{6})}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse hyperbolic sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{6})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{6}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{6}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=6\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+36}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{6})}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\cdot (6\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡1-\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+\\sqrt{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-96968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-96968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-96968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+\\sqrt{2})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+\\sqrt{6})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\sqrt{3})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\sqrt{6})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6+\\sqrt{3})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-96968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+\\sqrt{2})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95899" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95899" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4}}\\,\\text{d}x=4{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse hyperbolic sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{2}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=2\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\cdot (2\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}} \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2-8\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡0 \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2 \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+1}) \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\sqrt{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95899" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37c368262d375ac82f1030be97f52e3532e28b8944111f1b72cb56ec930b43fa"} {"question" "q-95899" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95899" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\sqrt{2})"] ["math" "8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\sqrt{5})"] ["math" "8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3+\\sqrt{5})"] ["math" "8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5+\\sqrt{2})"] ["math" "8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5+\\sqrt{3})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "q-95899" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\sqrt{5})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/state.json" "file_sha256" "e31d3b557303360850579cab966de9e0784c91a34506a3f13498f91891542a9e"} {"question" "e-8393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\pi}{\\sqrt{2x^2+1}} \\, \\textrm{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/example-8393.json" "file_sha256" "712e31065cddcb76c83bc05d9406a4b595379a419a6abb6dfaf681f1c7d16ee8"} {"question" "e-8393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u^2+1}}\\,\\textrm{d}u = \\arsinh u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u^2$ as the variable, we have $2x^2 = \\left(\\sqrt{2}\\,x\\right)^2.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u =\\sqrt{2}\\,x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=\\sqrt{2}\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\textrm{d}x = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\,\\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{2}\\,x)}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\pi \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{2}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{\\arsinh}u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{\\arsinh}(\\sqrt{2}\\,x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/example-8393.json" "file_sha256" "712e31065cddcb76c83bc05d9406a4b595379a419a6abb6dfaf681f1c7d16ee8"} {"question" "e-8394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\n$\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{3}{\\sqrt{x^2-4}} \\,\\textrm{d}x   =$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/example-8394.json" "file_sha256" "268716b0bf223be3b7f3de3ad108c4e0a89a4fed85a7cb8c37a3c0f516f3ffc6"} {"question" "e-8394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nLet's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{3}{\\sqrt{x^2-4}}\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\dfrac{3}{2} \\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^2-1}} \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u^2-1}}\\,\\textrm{d}u = \\arcosh u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u^2$ as the variable, we have $\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)^2.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u = \\dfrac x 2.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac{1}{2}\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\textrm{d}x =2\\,\\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =3\\text{\\arcosh}u+C \\\\  & =3\\text{\\arcosh}(\\frac{x}{2})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/example-8394.json" "file_sha256" "268716b0bf223be3b7f3de3ad108c4e0a89a4fed85a7cb8c37a3c0f516f3ffc6"} {"question" "e-8395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\n$\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{10}{1 - 4x^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x   =$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/example-8395.json" "file_sha256" "b82b18139738f5e53fd6da7661474c2bfe8e1f613daf2ce866fd80e45b56671c"} {"question" "e-8395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1-u^2} \\, \\textrm{d}u =\\artanh u +C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u^2$ as the variable, we have $4x^2 = \\left(2x\\right)^2.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=2x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 2\\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{10}{1-4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =10\\int \\frac{1}{1-(2x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5\\text{\\artanh}u+C \\\\  & =5\\text{\\artanh}2x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that this result is subject to the condition $\\left|2x \\right| <    1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/example-8395.json" "file_sha256" "b82b18139738f5e53fd6da7661474c2bfe8e1f613daf2ce866fd80e45b56671c"} {"question" "e-8396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nEvaluate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int_{4}^{2\\sqrt{5}} \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2 - 4}}\\, \\textrm{d}x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/example-8396.json" "file_sha256" "90d66c5a7bbe793790bcc4832beeaaf30ce446898bc0f8a8f67505459cb2c1e7"} {"question" "e-8396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nNote that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int_{4}^{2\\sqrt{5}} \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2 - 4}}\\, \\textrm{d}x = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\int_{4}^{2\\sqrt{5}} \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac {x}{2} \\right)^2 - 1}} \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u^2-1}}\\, \\textrm{d}u = \\arcosh{u}+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u^2$ as the variable, we have $\\left(\\dfrac {x}{2} \\right)^2.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u = \\dfrac {x}{2}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\textrm{d}x = 2\\,\\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $4$ | $2\\sqrt{5}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $\\sqrt{5}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\int_{4}^{2\\sqrt{5}} \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2 - 4}}\\, \\textrm{d}x &= \\dfrac{1}{2}\\int_{4}^{2\\sqrt{5}} \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac {x}{2} \\right)^2 - 1}} \\, \\textrm{d}x \\[5pt]\n\n&= \\dfrac{1}{2} \\int_{2}^{\\sqrt 5} \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{u^2 - 1}} \\cdot (2 \\, \\textrm{d}u) \\[5pt]\n\n&= \\int_{2}^{\\sqrt 5} \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\sqrt{u^2 - 1}} \\[5pt]\n\n&= \\arcosh u \\Big|_{2}^{\\sqrt 5} \\[5pt]\n\n&= \\arcosh{\\sqrt 5} - \\arcosh{2} \\[5pt]\n\n&=  \\ln\\left(\\sqrt 5 + \\sqrt{\\left(\\sqrt 5\\right)^2 - 1}\\right) - \\ln\\left(2 + \\sqrt{\\left(2\\right)^2 - 1}\\right)  \\[5pt]\n\n&= \\ln\\left(2 + \\sqrt{5}\\right) -  \\ln\\left(2 + \\sqrt{3}\\right)  \\[5pt]\n\n& = \\ln\\left(\\dfrac{2 + \\sqrt{5}}{2 + \\sqrt{3}}  \\right)\n\n}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/example-8396.json" "file_sha256" "90d66c5a7bbe793790bcc4832beeaaf30ce446898bc0f8a8f67505459cb2c1e7"} {"question" "q-95432" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡4x+C"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060281/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "40332e